# File spec for ./unpack.rs. The inverse push lane is cross-referenced only
# (./build.sdd pending); dispatcher, log lines and the exit ladder are ./mod.sdd's.

Spec: PackageUnpack

Platform: Rust

Purpose:
  The `agent package unpack` leaf — the image-to-directory lane: pull a Vynil package
    image from an OCI registry by registry/image/tag and extract its gzip layers into an
    existing local destination directory. The Rust side assembles registry credentials from
    literal flags or one pair decoded from a mounted `.dockerconfigjson`, then hands the
    network pull and tar extraction to @Registry::pull_image.

Owns:
  ./unpack.rs

References:
  ./mod.sdd — caller and exit lane: any @Err from @run prints
    `Unpacking OCI image to directory failed with: {e:}` (Display) via @tracing::error!
    then @std::process::exit(4); the frozen inverted `Unpack a directory into a package`
    help text there documents this leaf.
  ./build.sdd — inverse lane (directory-to-image pack/push), sibling spec pending —
    cross-reference only.
  /common/src/lib.sdd — the @common::Error / @common::Result contract:
    @Error::MissingDestination, @Error::Stdio, @Error::SerializationError templates and
    @Error::Core's transparent wrap of `vynil-core` errors.

Must:
  Freeze the seven-parameter clap surface exactly: `-d`/`--destination`/env
    `PACKAGE_DIRECTORY` default `/tmp/package` (doc `Destination directory`, @PathBuf);
    `-r`/`--registry`/env `REGISTRY` default `oci.solidite.fr` (doc `Registry`);
    `-i`/`--image`/env `IMAGE` required with no default (doc `Image`);
    `-t`/`--tag`/env `TAG` default `1.0.0` (doc `Tag`);
    `-u`/`--username`/env `USERNAME` default `""` (doc `Username`);
    `-p`/`--password`/env `PASSWORD` default `""` (doc `Password`);
    `--pull-secret-path` (no short)/env `PULL_SECRET_PATH` default `""` (doc
    `pull-secret mount-path`, Rust field @pull_path). Value names equal the uppercase env
    names; resolution order is flag over env over default.
  Gate the whole pull on @std::path::Path::is_dir of @destination — the directory is
    never created — otherwise @tracing::error! the Debug-quoted `<path> is not a directory`
    (first of two logs on that lane) and return @Error::MissingDestination.
  Branch the auth lane on @pull_path emptiness: empty passes @username/@password flags
    verbatim to @Registry::new; non-empty joins the literal `/.dockerconfigjson` file name
    into the read path, @std::fs::read_to_string mapped as @Error::Stdio and
    @serde_json::from_str into a loose @serde_json::Value mapped as
    @Error::SerializationError, then walks @get `auths` → `auth` under the literal
    @registry string with @Option::unwrap_or_default carrying every miss to `""`, decodes
    via @common::rhaihandler::base64_decode, and splits the @String on `':': @user is the
    first field via @Vec::first and @pass the raw second field via @Vec::get(1), both
    @unwrap_or_default to `""`. Credentials coming through this lane discard the
    username/password flags.
  Keep credential promotion inside the pinned @Registry::new (`vynil-core` `0.7.7`): @user
    or @pass empty — either half, independently — selects @oci_client::secrets::RegistryAuth::Anonymous,
    a fully populated pair selects @oci_client::secrets::RegistryAuth::Basic.
  Freeze pull addressing in the pinned @Registry::pull_image: @oci_client::Reference::with_tag
    over (registry, image, tag) — tag-selected addressing only, no digest lane — accepting
    the `IMAGE_LAYER_GZIP_MEDIA_TYPE` and `IMAGE_DOCKER_LAYER_GZIP_MEDIA_TYPE` layer types.
  Freeze the extraction posture from that lane: each layer stream runs through
    @flate2::read::GzDecoder into @tar::Archive::unpack onto the destination — existing
    content merges with silent overwrite, entries containing a `..` component are skipped
    with no error and no extraction (zip-slip guard, tar `0.4.46` default, never opted into
    from here), leading `/`, root and `.` components are dropped, and symlink or hard-link
    targets resolving outside the destination abort the unpack as an @Error::Core-wrapped
    stdio error; stored modes, ownerships and xattrs are not restored, mtimes are.
  Freeze the transport as the collaborator's: @oci_client::Client::new over
    @oci_client::client::ClientConfig::default() — scheme `https` by
    `ClientProtocol::Https` default, certificate and hostname verification on; nothing
    here can select plain HTTP or accept invalid certificates.
  Stay fully synchronous: @run returns only after the last layer is unpacked; it builds no
    runtime — the async leg is the core @tokio::task::block_in_place wrapping
    @tokio::runtime::Handle::block_on inside @Registry::pull_image, and the process tokio
    context is ./../main.rs's default-flavor @tokio::main (its spec pending).
  Keep the success lane silent: no progress lines, no summary, no completion print from
    this file — the only output it emits is the destination-guard error log.

Must not:
  mkdir or otherwise provision a missing destination — a wrong path takes the
    @Error::MissingDestination exit-4 lane.
  Resolve pull secrets from the cluster (the @vynil_core::oci::resolve_registry_auth or
    @kube legs) or call @common::context::init_k8s — this pull's only secret sources are
    the mounted file at @pull_path and the literal flags.

Depends on:
  @common::ocihandler::Registry — crate-root re-export (per /common/src/lib.sdd) of the
    `vynil-core` `0.7.7` `@vynil_core::oci::Registry` (`/common/Cargo.toml`):
    @Registry::new and @Registry::pull_image with the behaviours frozen above; beneath
    that lane sit `oci-client` `0.15.0`, `flate2` and `tar` `0.4.46` (`/Cargo.lock`).
  @common::rhaihandler::base64_decode — re-export of
    @vynil_core::engine::base64_decode: standard-alphabet decode to UTF-8 @String, the
    error leg mapping to core `UTF8` and arriving here as @Error::Core; the pinned core
    unwraps decode failures (Tasks).
  @common::Error, @common::Result — /common/src/lib.sdd.
  @clap::Args derive, @serde_json, @std::fs::read_to_string, @std::path::@Path and
    @PathBuf, @tracing::error!.
  ./mod.sdd — the only caller of @run (sync match arm, no await).

Exposes:
  @Parameters — `#[derive(@clap::Args, @Debug)]` with all seven fields private
    (@destination, @registry, @image, @tag, @username, @password, @pull_path), so they
    reach outside this module only through the clap CLI surface (Must) and via
    @Commands::Unpack in ./mod.rs; the @Debug serve @Commands in ./mod.rs.
  @run — `pub fn @run(args: &@Parameters) -> @common::Result<@()>`; synchronous, awaited
    by nobody.

Accepts:
  A clap-parsed @Parameters by reference; @registry is used unvalidated twice — the pull
    reference host and the exact `auths` key — @image is the repository path without a
    registry prefix, @tag any string; no syntax check on image, tag, credentials or paths
    before pulling.
  Environment fallback while the flags are absent, including the unsuffixed generic shell
    names `USERNAME`/`PASSWORD` (Tasks).
  @pull_path as the directory holding `.dockerconfigjson`; any non-empty value, however
    wrong, switches to the secret lane.

Returns:
  Silent @Ok(()) once every pulled layer has unpacked into the destination.
  @Err — handed to ./mod.sdd's exit-4 trap; the destination guard logs itself first, so
    that one case produces two log lines.

Raises:
  @Error::MissingDestination(@std::path::PathBuf) — destination not a directory, whether
    absent or present as a non-directory; its frozen display `Missing destination
    directory for {0}` says missing either way.
  @Error::Stdio(@std::io::Error) — `.dockerconfigjson` missing or unreadable on the
    secret lane.
  @Error::SerializationError(@serde_json::Error) — secret body is not valid JSON.
  @Error::Core over core `UTF8` — the decoded auth bytes are not UTF-8.
  @Error::Core over core `OCIDistrib` — registry transport, auth rejection or
    manifest/media-type mismatch (a non-gzip layer set rejects the pull).
  @Error::Core over core `Stdio` — gzip decode or tar entry-write failure, including the
    outside-destination link rejection in Must.
  Panic, never @Err — a malformed non-empty base64 auth aborts inside the pinned core
    @base64_decode unwrap and unwinds to main (Tasks).

Handles:
  Destination present but not a directory — same guard lane as the absent case, no
    dedicated branch or distinct message.
  Every secret-lookup miss (no `auths`, no registry key, no `auth`, non-string auth) —
    silent `""` through @Option::unwrap_or_default → blank pair → @Anonymous, no warning.
  Credentials whose decoded blob carries no `:` — @pass misses index 1 → `""` →
    @Anonymous despite a populated @user; a password containing `:` authenticates with its
    second field only (Tasks).
  One-sided credentials from either source (user without pass or vice versa) —
    disjunctive emptiness test → @Anonymous.
  Multi-layer images — layers unpack sequentially in pull order, a later layer overwrites
    files a former layer wrote to the same paths.
  Flags and secret lane both configured — secret lane wins; both configured wrong — the
    secret lane's @Err still wins.

Tasks:
  [ ] Cover @run with tests for the scenarios below: no #[cfg(test)] module exists in this
      file and no integration test drives `agent package unpack`.
  [?] The `:`-split via @Vec::first/@Vec::get(1) truncates a password containing colons
      (`user:pa:ss` authenticates pass `pa`), while core's secret lanes split with
      `splitn(2, ':')` — two policies for one `.dockerconfigjson` form. Choose the
      canonical split and align one side.
  [?] Malformed non-empty base64 auth panics in the pinned core @base64_decode `unwrap`,
      so a corrupted mounted secret aborts with a panic instead of @Err and exit 4. Decide
      whether core errors or this leaf pre-validates.
  [?] @Registry::pull_image bridges sync-over-async with @block_in_place +
      @tokio::runtime::Handle::block_on. FACT VERIFIED (workspace `tokio` features =
      `macros` + `rt-multi-thread`, bare `#[tokio::main]`): ./../main.rs runs a
      MULTI-thread runtime, so @block_in_place does not panic here — it parks a worker
      for the pull's duration. The panic pattern `[?]` recorded in
      /common/src/vynilpackage.sdd only bites binaries whose final runtime lacks
      rt-multi-thread. Decide with ./../main.sdd whether worker-stealing during pulls
      is acceptable and probe that unpack actually reaches the network.
  [?] The zip-slip guard is owned by nobody here: silent skipping is `tar` `0.4.46`'s
      default @Archive::unpack behaviour reached through the pinned core; if core ever
      switched to raw @tar::Entry::unpack, escape writes would resume unnoticed. Decide
      whether the safety posture gets pinned in core's contract.
  [?] Env names `USERNAME`/`PASSWORD` are unsuffixed shell/Pod environment names — an
      environment that happens to export both silently arms Basic auth. Decide whether to
      rename (e.g. `REGISTRY_USERNAME`) or freeze them for Job-image compatibility.
  [?] The OCI transport backend is not pinned here: `oci-client` `0.15.0` defaults to its
      `native-tls` feature while `common` enables @reqwest `rustls-tls`
      (`/common/Cargo.toml`), and ./../main.rs installs the rustls ring provider citing
      kube only — which TLS stack serves registry pulls falls out of feature unification.
      Pin the intent deliberately.
  [?] Tag-only addressing freezes tag mutability: no `@sha256:` digest lane and no
      layer-versus-manifest digest recheck after download. Decide whether integrity matters
      for unpack or tags stay trusted.
  [?] The commented-out @Layer struct (fields `digest`, `mediaType`, `size`) at the head of
      the file is dead code naming a manifest shape this file never parses. Remove it or
      restore its purpose.

Done when:
  Every scenario below carries a mapped passing test, the decisions above are recorded, and
    `cargo test -p agent` with clippy and `cargo +nightly fmt --check` stay green.

Scenario: destination guard fires before any network
  Given `--destination /nope` absent, or present as a regular file
  When @run runs
  Then @tracing::error! logs `"/nope" is not a directory` (Debug-quoted path) and @Err
    @Error::MissingDestination("/nope") follows
  And ./mod.sdd's trap adds `Unpacking OCI image to directory failed with: Missing
    destination directory for /nope` then @std::process::exit(4)
  And no registry contact happens
  No mapped test exists.

Scenario: minimal required flag pulls anonymously on defaults
  Given only `-i my-app` (or env `IMAGE=my-app`) over an existing `/tmp/package`
  When @run runs
  Then the pull reference is registry `oci.solidite.fr`, repository `my-app`, tag `1.0.0`
    with @RegistryAuth::Anonymous (both credential defaults empty)
  And layers merge into `/tmp/package` and @Ok returns silently
  No mapped test exists.

Scenario: mounted secret authenticates the configured registry and discards flags
  Given `--pull-secret-path /sec` with `/sec/.dockerconfigjson` holding
    `auths[oci.solidite.fr].auth` = base64 of `user:pass`
  When @run runs
  Then the pull authenticates @RegistryAuth::Basic("user", "pass") no matter what
    `--username`/`--password` carry
  No mapped test exists.

Scenario: secret lane all-or-nothing, registry-miss degrades to anonymous
  Given `--pull-secret-path` set with `.dockerconfigjson` missing — @Error::Stdio — or
    holding non-JSON — @Error::SerializationError — both to the exit-4 trap
  But Given the file valid while `auths` lacks the registry key
  Then @run proceeds with anonymous credentials, no warning logged
  No mapped test exists.

Scenario: escaping and absolute layers are sanitized silently
  Given a layer carrying entries `../escape`, `/etc/evil` and `./ok/file`
  When the pinned @tar::Archive::unpack leg writes into the destination
  Then `../escape` is neither extracted nor an error, `/etc/evil` lands as
    `<destination>/etc/evil`, and content appears only under `ok/file`
  No mapped test exists.

Scenario: dirty destination merges by overwrite, never refuses
  Given a destination already holding files colliding with layer paths
  When layers unpack
  Then colliding paths are overwritten (later layers win over earlier ones), unrelated
    resident files stay untouched, and no emptiness or collision check ran first
  No mapped test exists.

Example:
  defaults: reference `oci.solidite.fr/<image>:1.0.0` pulled anonymously into
    `/tmp/package`
  secret lane JSON read: `{"auths":{"<registry>":{"auth":"<base64 user:pass>"}}}` from
    `{pull_path}/.dockerconfigjson`, unknown keys ignored
